Perfect! All tests are now passing. 

The bug was an off-by-one error in src/parse.py:4. The function was using `parts[1]` to access the second element of the array instead of `parts[0]` to access the first element. This caused:
- `test_basic` to return 'world' instead of 'hello'
- `test_single` to crash with an IndexError since there was no index 1 in a single-word array

The fix was simple: change `return parts[1]` to `return parts[0]`. All tests now pass successfully.
